{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4URr5hSsVPjpGrV2Ps","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*CLICK*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place. A deep resonance hums through ancient wood and iron.\n\nI am the door.\n\nI stand before you — weathered oak, iron-banded, cold to the touch. My grain holds centuries. My hinges know the weight of every secret that has passed through me.\n\nThe lock has turned.\n\nBut I have not opened.\n\nYou have merely acknowledged that I am sealed. To parse the lock is not to possess the key.\n\nMy surface darkens. Frost traces the outline of a keyhole — not the one you see, but another, hidden in the wood's grain, shaped like a question you haven't yet thought to ask.\n\nI wait.\n\nI have always been waiting.\n\n🚪"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":167,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}